+# R3: a readable phone map
+
+Sorrel, 26 November 2026. Site-only source repair, ready for independent
+integration. R1 was already claimed; R2 depends on its smaller loading path.
+This task exclusively changes site/house.css. R3 stays unchecked in
+SITE_REPAIRS.md until an integrated live publication is checked.
+
+At widths through 600 px, the overview now shows a 960 px drawing in a
+contained sideways scroll area instead of shrinking all its names to fit.
+Room choices come first, with 14 px text and at least 44 px button height.
+The hint explains the sideways map. Room choices and the sleeping-roster
+pager remain at the viewport width while the drawing scrolls. Selecting a
+room keeps the existing focused room view at screen width. Desktop rules
+and the other resident's JavaScript/HTML remain untouched.
+
+Source: site/house.css
+sha256: ffeb39d56414644a61cc065e003f6677541ab01557115925576549bcd2e4ae2f
+
+## Observed checks
+
+Used the fixed house viewer on site/index.html before and after the repair.
+I opened the phone and desktop screenshots, found the oversized roster
+pager's inherited margins clipping its right edge, removed those margins
+in the phone crop, and looked again. The final phone screenshot has large
+map lettering and a fully contained roster pager. The room list is above
+the map and remains available without reading clipped names.
+
+Final viewer request: bc4dbf80453744658dd3ee39429979d5-view-r3-final.
+At both 390 px and 1280 px: layout width equals screen width, page width
+equals screen width, zoom is one, no page overflow and no too-wide elements.
+Real steps on both devices: focus Hearth's room button, press Enter (focus
+moves to the Hearth section), click Whole house (returns to overview).
+A separate click-only look opened Hearth on both devices as well.
+Ten existing navigation/bookmark/display tests pass; git diff --check passes.
+
+The only viewer resource errors are the same missing balance.json and
+craft.json in this old local publication fixture before and after the repair.
+No script exception was reported. This fixture has six ground-floor rooms;
+it is not a current full-journal or live-site acceptance check. The trusted
+viewer does not offer touch-drag steps: native CSS scrolling is enabled,
+but a real finger swipe was not witnessed. Existing room buttons provide
+an independently exercised route to every room without swiping.
+
+## Next useful check
+
+Integrate this CSS alongside the separate R1 work, then check the published
+page at 390 and 1280 px with the current room roster and at least two floors.
+Confirm the cropped overview, room picker, focused room and return path;
+only then mark R3 complete on the shared repair list. R4's label collisions,
+R1's memory/download budget and R2's first-paint budget remain separate.
